A1. This is full of ticks. ~ CLOCK
A5. A wet blanket. ~ FOG
A8. The limb that men forget. ~ SCRAG
A12. What your nose did during the rainy season. ~ RAN
A13. This picks up the news. ~ EAR
A14. And still more. ~ TOO
A15. This usually precedes hell. ~ AW
A16. Exist. ~ BE
A17. To manage somehow. ~ EKE
A18. What we'll all do sooner or later for what we're doing now. ~ ATONE
A20. An egotist's opinion of himself. ~ GREAT
A22. To put on a bad act. ~ ERR
A24. When this runs high you run low. ~ SEA
A25. A bad place for ships to land. ~ SHOALS
A26. What the gourmet did on Christmas eve. ~ ATE
A27. An old-fashioned windup. ~ STEM
A28. Subsists. ~ IS
A29. In the end husbands always do this. ~ ASSENT
A31. A typical corporation head. ~ BALD
A34. An old life-boat. ~ ARK
A35. Senior members as in a diplomatic corps. ~ DOYENS
A39. Before. ~ ERE
A40. The way she speaks of her husband, the hussy! ~ HIM
A41. Still at it. ~ YET
A42. A visible means of support. ~ TEE
A43. Led on but slapped. ~ TEASED
A45. A short teddy. ~ TED
A46. This should satisfy anyone. ~ SATE
A47. How a chorus girl makes up. ~ PREENS
A49. It abbreviated. ~ SA
A50. What little girls do at night before going to bed. ~ PRAY
A53. This will expose the calves. ~ RAT
A54. The best after-dinner speeches. ~ UNTOLD
A57. What candy pullers pull when they go fishing. ~ OAR
A58. You'll have to use a lot of pull to get along with this. ~ ASS
A59. There's a point to this holdup at the opera. ~ SPEAR
A60. What a Scotch midget is. ~ SMALL
A62. What you'll be till the doctor comes. ~ ILL
A64. This article is indefinite. ~ AN
A65. Thusly. ~ SO
A66. A kind of stinging line. ~ BEE
A67. A glass one looks good but doesn't look good. ~ EYE
A68. You dress to kill for this. ~ WAR
A69. These are red in Russia. ~ ROSES
A70. The kind of skin an Indian loves to touch. ~ RED
A71. Poor man's elevator. ~ STEPS

D1. Moving pinchers. ~ CRABS
D2. What usually gets broken at drinking places? ~ LAW
D3. Where the Prince of Wales has been staying recently. ~ ON
D4. What a prayer does in church. ~ KNEELS
D5. Get these firmly in the ground and watch yourself rise. ~ FEET
D6. This spreads itself all over the countryside. ~ OAK
D7. Glad hands. ~ GREETS
D8. This puts the sun to bed. ~ STAR
D9. You can trust a sentry to go to sleep here. ~ COT
D10. Chickens get all up in the air over this. ~ ROOST
D11. What the bright lights do for the pleasure seeker. ~ GLEAM
D16. This will trim anything. ~ BRAID
D19. Born. ~ NEE
D20. What to do if you get the chance to go to Paris. ~ GO
D21. Since. ~ AS
