D34. Helping hands. ~ AIDERS
D36. A crossword in Greek. ~ ETA
D37. Old-fashioned rat-trap. ~ NET
D38. Good lookers do this. ~ SEE
D40. The way he speaks of his wife, the dog! ~ HER
D41. Affirmative. ~ YES
D44. A good looker ~ SPY
D45. A little bit of this goes a long way (abbr.). ~ TNT
D46. A hell of a fellow. ~ SATAN
D48. Not so tough. ~ EASIER
D49. Prowlers. ~ SNEAKS
D50. This'll stump you. ~ POSER
D51. A good butter. ~ RAM
D52. Camels walk many miles for these. ~ ARABS
D54. If you go this way you're bound to rise. ~ UP
D55. Conjunction. ~ OR
D56. These are good for a grand slam. ~ DOORS
